<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan Chih Lien plans T$800 mln investment.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Chih Lien plans T$800 mln investment.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's Chih Lien Industry will invest T$800 million in a drive to double its plant's steel rod and wire capacity by 1998, company officials said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Chih Lien's plant expansion, to be completed by 1998, would double annual production capacity to 10,000 tonnes, an executive said by telephone.</p>
<p>The expansion would make Chih Lien Taiwan's largest steel rod and wire producer, local media said.</p>
<p>Company officials declined to comment on expansion details.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-508-0815)</p>
</text>
